Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 10 — WebView & Progressive Web App (PWA) Android Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand Android applications built around WebView, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, or Progressive Web Apps (PWAs). Unlike native applications, these apps execute much of their logic inside a browser engine embedded within Android. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct the web application architecture, browser runtime, communication with Android, offline behavior, storage, rendering, and lifecycle.



> Core Principle:
A WebView application is simultaneously an Android application and a web application. Reverse engineer both environments and their communication.




