Stage 27 — Common WebView Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating the WebView as just another Android View.

Ignoring the browser engine and JavaScript runtime.

Confusing browser lifecycle with Android lifecycle.

Overlooking Service Workers in PWAs.

Ignoring JavaScript ↔ Android bridge communication.

Treating browser storage as equivalent to Android persistence.

Producing separate Android and web architectures instead of one integrated model.



---

Stage 28 — WebView & PWA Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify WebView, PWA, and hybrid web-based Android applications.

✅ Reconstruct HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and browser architecture alongside the Android host.

✅ Recover routing, state management, rendering, browser storage, and Service Worker behavior.

✅ Understand communication between JavaScript and Android through native bridges.

✅ Correlate browser lifecycle with Android lifecycle and validate the combined execution model.

✅ Produce a unified architectural model covering both the web application and its Android integration.



